    "methods_description": "EEG signals were recorded using a 64-channel Synamps RT system (Neuroscan) at three timepoints (pre-, mid-, and post-tests) while participants performed a distractor version of the change detection task with three conditions (2T0D, 4T0D, 2T2D). Vertical and horizontal electrooculograms (EOGs) were recorded to monitor eye movements. The reference electrode was placed on the left mastoid with electrode impedance maintained below 5kΩ. Behavioral data were collected from a multi-object change detection task and a suppress task.",
